ons-in-2025", "label": "TeslaNorth, citing SpaceX filing to the FCC"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "threshold", "eyebrow": "Who decides", "title": "Each operator sets its own threshold", "body": "Operators choose when a close pass is worth a move. SpaceX moves at three in ten million; the common standard is one in 10,000.", "sources": [{"url": "https://teslanorth.com/2026/01/25/starlink-satellites-made-300000-moves-to-avoid-collisions-in-2025", "label": "TeslaNorth, citing SpaceX filing to the FCC"}]}, {"kind": "numberSense", "id": "ns-moves", "prompt": "About how many collision-avoidance maneuvers did Starlink make in 2025, in thousands?", "min": 0, "max": 800, "value": 300, "unit": "k", "explanation": "About 300,000, nearly 40 per satellite."}, {"kind": "theCall", "id": "call", "situation": "You run a 300-satellite network. A Starlink satellite may pass close to one of yours tomorrow.", "prompt": "What do you do?", "options": ["Assume they will dodge and do nothing", "Contact SpaceX and agree on who moves", "Move every satellite to a new orbit"], "consequences": ["If both sides assume the other moves, nobody does.", "Agreeing who moves avoids a double swerve, or none at all.", "Moving a whole fleet burns fuel over one close pass."], "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "Close passes are routine now. Talking to the other operator avoids both of you moving, or neither."}, {"id": "lens-invest", "kind": "info", "title": "Crowding is a cost", "body": "More maneuvers mean more fuel and more staff time. As orbits fill, operating costs rise for everyone.", "eyebrow": "For investors", "sources": [{"url": "https://teslanorth.com/2026/01/25/starlink-satellites-made-300000-moves-to-avoid-collisions-in-2025", "label": "TeslaNorth, citing SpaceX filing to the FCC"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In space, crowded orbits turn safety into a daily operating cost.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://teslanorth.com/2026/01/25/starlink-satellites-made-300000-moves-to-avoid-collisions-in-2025", "label": "TeslaNorth, citing SpaceX filing to the FCC"}, {"url": "https://space.com/spacex-starlink-50000-collision-avoidance-maneuvers-space-safety", "label": "Space.com, 50,000 maneuvers in six months"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "Starlink made about 300,000 collision-avoidance maneuvers in 2025, up from about 25,000 per half-year in 2023. Each operator sets its own risk threshold.", "sectionKey": "review"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
