ollisions-in-2025", "label": "TeslaNorth, citing SpaceX filing to the FCC"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "threshold", "eyebrow": "Who decides", "title": "Each operator sets its own threshold", "body": "Operators choose when a close pass is worth a move. SpaceX moves at three in ten million; the common standard is one in 10,000.", "sources": [{"url": "https://teslanorth.com/2026/01/25/starlink-satellites-made-300000-moves-to-avoid-collisions-in-2025", "label": "TeslaNorth, citing SpaceX filing to the FCC"}]}, {"kind": "numberSense", "id": "ns-moves", "prompt": "About how many collision-avoidance maneuvers did Starlink make in 2025, in thousands?", "min": 0, "max": 800, "value": 300, "unit": "k", "explanation": "About 300,000, nearly 40 per satellite."}, {"kind": "theCall", "id": "call", "situation": "You run a 300-satellite network. A Starlink satellite may pass close to one of yours tomorrow.", "prompt": "What do you do?", "options": ["Assume they will dodge and do nothing", "Contact SpaceX and agree on who moves", "Move every satellite to a new orbit"], "consequences": ["If both sides assume the other moves, nobody does.", "Agreeing who moves avoids a double swerve, or none at all.", "Moving a whole fleet burns fuel over one close pass."], "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "Close passes are routine now. Talking to the other operator avoids both of you moving, or neither."}, {"id": "lens-curiosity", "kind": "info", "title": "Swerving 800 times a day", "body": "300,000 maneuvers in a year is more than 800 every day.", "eyebrow": "Why it matters", "sources": [{"url": "https://teslanorth.com/2026/01/25/starlink-satellites-made-300000-moves-to-avoid-collisions-in-2025", "label": "TeslaNorth, citing SpaceX filing to the FCC"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In space, crowded orbits turn safety into a daily operating cost.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://teslanorth.com/2026/01/25/starlink-satellites-made-300000-moves-to-avoid-collisio