y.com/sustainability/2024/05/01/slingshot-aerospace-reveals-record-insurance-losses-in-2023-in-new-satellite-deployments-report", "label": "Via Satellite, record space insurance losses in 2023"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In space, insurers price the risk, and one bad year resets the price for everyone.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.satellitetoday.com/sustainability/2024/05/01/slingshot-aerospace-reveals-record-insurance-losses-in-2023-in-new-satellite-deployments-report", "label": "Via Satellite, record space insurance losses in 2023"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "In 2023, insurers paid $995 million in space claims against about $557 million in premiums. Rates for a geostationary satellite rose from under 6% to about 10%.", "sectionKey": "drivers"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$0045491b-43b7-5096-9357-c890f494b759$ml$::uuid, $ml$spacetech$ml$, $ml$When satellites fail, insurers pay$ml$, 'LESSON', ARRAY[$ml$MICRO_LESSON$ml$, $ml$day-14$ml$, $ml$month-1$ml$, $ml$handwritten-v1$ml$, $ml$goal:build_startup$ml$, $ml$level:beginner$ml$, $ml$level:intermediate$ml$, $ml$level:advanced$ml$]::text[], 5, now(), '{}'::jsonb, $ml${"id": "spacetech-d14-build_startup", "title": "When satellites fail, insurers pay", "exercises": [{"id": "open", "kind": "coldOpen", "kicker": "One bad year wiped out the profits.", "eyebrow": "Day 14 · The money", "headline": "In 2023, space insurers paid $995 million in claims but collected only about $557 million.", "fullText": "Two satellites caused most of the damage: ViaSat-3 Americas led to a $445 million claim and Inmarsat-6 F2, after a battery failure, to $348 million. The net loss of $438 million was a record. The premium for a typical geostationary satellite on a Falcon 9 rose from under 6% of its insured value to about 10%.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.satellitetoday.com/sustainability/2024/05/01/slingshot-aerospace-reveals-record-insurance-losses-in-2023-in-new-satellite-deployments-report", "label": "Via Satellite, record space insurance losses in 2023"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "premium", "eyebrow": "How it works", "text": "Operators pay a premium: a share of the satellite's insured value.", "highlight": "For a geostationary satellite on Falcon 9, it rose from under 6% to about 10% in 2023.", "keyTerms": [{"term": "Premium", "definition": "What an operator pays an insurer, often quoted as a percent of insured value."}], "sources": [{"url": "https://www.satellitetoday.com/sustainability/2024/05/01/slingshot-aerospace-reveals-record-insurance-losses-in-2023-in-new-satellite-deployments-report", "label": "Via Satellite, record space insurance losses in 2023"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "big-bets", "eyebrow": "The concentration", "text": "A few big satellites carry most of the risk.", "highlight": "Two claims, $445 million and $348 million, made 2023 a record loss.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.satellitetoday.com/sustainability/2024/05/01/slingshot-aerospace-reveals-record-insurance-losses-in-2023-in-new-satellite-deployments-report", "label": "Via Satellite, record space insurance losses in 2023"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "exits", "eyebrow": "The aftermath", "title": "Some insurers walked away", "body": "After 2023, some insurers left the space market completely. Fewer insurers means less capacity and higher prices.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.satellitetoday.com/sustainability/2024/05/01/slingshot-aerospace-reveals-record-insurance-losses-in-2023-in-new-satellite-deployments-report", "label": "Via Satellite, record space insurance losses in 2023"}]}, {"kind": "numberSense", "id": "ns-loss", "prompt": "Space insurers paid $995 million in 2023 claims and collected about $557 million in premiums. What was the loss, in millions of dollars?", "min": 0, "max": 1000, "value": 438, "unit": "M", "explanation": "$995 million minus $557 million is about $438 million, a record."}, {"kind": "theCall", "id": "call", "situation": "You are about to launch a $300 million geostationary satellite. Premiums just jumped to about 10%.", "prompt": "What do you do?", "options": ["Fly uninsured to save the premium", "Delay the launch until premiums fall", "Insure it and budget the higher premium"], "consequences": ["One failure could sink the company.", "Every month on the ground delays revenue, and prices may not fall.", "About $30 million protects a $300 million asset."], "correctIndex": 2, "explanation": "Few operators can absorb losing a $300 million satellite. The premium is the price of surviving a failure."}, {"id": "lens-build_startup", "kind": "info", "title": "Better risk data has buyers", "body": "Insurers lost $438 million in one year. Anything that predicts failures better is worth paying for.", "eyebrow": "For founders", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.satellitetoday.com/sustainability/2024/05/01/slingshot-aerospace-reveals-record-insurance-losses-in-2023-in-new-satellite-deployments-report", "label": "Via Satellite, record space insurance losses in 2023"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In space, insurers price the risk, and one bad year resets the price for everyone.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.satellitetoday.com/sustainability/2024/05/01/slingshot-aerospace-reveals-record-insurance-losses-in-2023-in-new-satellite-deployments-report", "label": "Via Satellite, record space insurance losses in 2023"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "In 2023, insurers paid $995 million in space claims against about $557 million in premiums. Rates for a geostationary satellite rose from under 6% to about 10%.", "sectionKey": "gap"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
