($ml$cbbcb0a6-41b4-506a-8a5c-ab3ab5ce6bf6$ml$::uuid, $ml$spacetech$ml$, $ml$The launch company that ran out of money$ml$, 'LESSON', ARRAY[$ml$MICRO_LESSON$ml$, $ml$day-18$ml$, $ml$month-1$ml$, $ml$handwritten-v1$ml$, $ml$goal:career$ml$, $ml$level:beginner$ml$, $ml$level:intermediate$ml$, $ml$level:advanced$ml$]::text[], 5, now(), '{}'::jsonb, $ml${"id": "spacetech-d18-career", "title": "The launch company that ran out of money", "exercises": [{"id": "open", "kind": "coldOpen", "kicker": "More than $1 billion, six launches.", "eyebrow": "Day 18 · Where it breaks", "headline": "Virgin Orbit filed for bankruptcy in April 2023, three months after a failed launch from the UK.", "fullText": "Virgin Orbit dropped small rockets from under the wing of a Boeing 747. Investors put in more than $1 billion, but it flew only six times and lost $191.1 million in 2022. After the January 2023 failure, the first orbital attempt from UK soil, it laid off all but 100 of its nearly 800 staff and filed for Chapter 11.", "sources": [{"url": "https://thespacereview.com/article/4593/1", "label": "The Space Review, death of a launch company"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "math", "eyebrow": "The math", "text": "Small launchers face hard math: few flights, high fixed costs.", "highlight": "Virgin Orbit lost about $50 million a quarter.", "sources": [{"url": "https://thespacereview.com/article/4593/1", "label": "The Space Review, death of a launch company"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "auction", "eyebrow": "The end", "text": "Its assets sold for about $36.5 million at auction.", "highlight": "Rocket Lab paid $16.1 million for its factory; Stratolaunch $17 million for the 747.", "sources": [{"url": "https://thespacereview.com/article/4593/1", "label": "The Space Review, death of a launch company"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "squeeze", "eyebrow": "The squeeze", "title": "Cheap rideshare squeezes small rockets", "body": "Small satellites can share a big rocket at about $7,000 per kg. A dedicated small launch has to win on timing and orbit.", "sources": [{"url": "https://newspaceeconomy.ca/2026/02/27/satellite-ridesharing-market-analysis-2026/", "label": "New Space Economy, rideshare market 2026"}]}, {"kind": "multipleChoice", "id": "mc", "prompt": "What does Virgin Orbit's collapse show about small launch?", "options": ["Launching from a jet can never reach orbit", "Too few flights cannot cover high fixed costs", "Governments banned small rockets in 2023"], "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "Six flights could not support a company losing about $50 million a quarter."}, {"kind": "faceOff", "id": "face", "prompt": "A 100 kg satellite needs to reach a common orbit soon. Which ride usually wins?", "left": {"name": "A dedicated small rocket", "note": "Your own launch, at a higher price per kg"}, "right": {"name": "A rideshare seat", "note": "About $7,000 per kg, shared"}, "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "If the rideshare orbit works, its lower price wins. Small rockets win when timing or orbit matter more."}, {"id": "lens-career", "kind": "info", "title": "Ask how a launcher breaks even", "body": "Ask how many flights a year a launch company needs to cover its costs. It is the question that sank Virgin Orbit.", "eyebrow": "For your interview", "sources": [{"url": "https://thespacereview.com/article/4593/1", "label": "The Space Review, death of a launch company"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In launch, flying too rarely can sink even a well-funded company.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://thespacereview.com/article/4593/1", "label": "The Space Review, death of a launch company"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "Virgin Orbit raised more than $1 billion but flew only six times and went bankrupt in 2023. Small launchers must fly often or offer what rideshare can't.", "sectionKey": "my_view"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
