 work its companies will win in the next years.", "eyebrow": "For investors", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}, {"url": "https://spacepolicyonline.com/?p=85281", "label": "SpacePolicyOnline, ESA members pledge record funding"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In European space, where the money comes from decides where the work goes.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}, {"url": "https://europeanspaceflight.com/esa-director-general-reaffirms-geo-return-policy-as-fundamental/", "label": "European Spaceflight, geo-return reaffirmed"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "ESA members pledged a record €22.07 billion in November 2025. Geo-return sends contracts back to each country roughly in proportion to what it pays.", "sectionKey": "drivers"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$b8e95f02-34bc-582b-b88f-c358ebf9cf85$ml$::uuid, $ml$spacetech$ml$, $ml$Every euro comes home$ml$, 'LESSON', ARRAY[$ml$MICRO_LESSON$ml$, $ml$day-20$ml$, $ml$month-1$ml$, $ml$handwritten-v1$ml$, $ml$goal:build_startup$ml$, $ml$level:beginner$ml$, $ml$level:intermediate$ml$, $ml$level:advanced$ml$]::text[], 5, now(), '{}'::jsonb, $ml${"id": "spacetech-d20-build_startup", "title": "Every euro comes home", "exercises": [{"id": "open", "kind": "coldOpen", "kicker": "Pay in, and your companies get the work.", "eyebrow": "Day 20 · The money", "headline": "In November 2025, ESA's members pledged a record €22.07 billion for the next three years.", "fullText": "That was 32% more than in 2022, or 17% after inflation. Under ESA's geographical return rule, contracts flow back to each country's industry roughly in proportion to what it pays in. The rule gives countries a reason to contribute, but critics say it adds cost and slows programs.", "sources": [{"url": "https://spacepolicyonline.com/?p=85281", "label": "SpacePolicyOnline, ESA members pledge record funding"}, {"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}, {"url": "https://europeanspaceflight.com/esa-director-general-reaffirms-geo-return-policy-as-fundamental/", "label": "European Spaceflight, geo-return reaffirmed"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "ratio", "eyebrow": "The rule", "text": "Geo-return aims for a ratio of 1: a country's share of contracts matches its share of funding.", "highlight": "In practice, ratios run between 0.9 and 0.95 over five years.", "keyTerms": [{"term": "Geo-return", "definition": "ESA's rule that contracts go to each country's industry in proportion to its funding."}], "sources": [{"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}, {"url": "https://europeanspaceflight.com/esa-director-general-reaffirms-geo-return-policy-as-fundamental/", "label": "European Spaceflight, geo-return reaffirmed"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "per-program", "eyebrow": "The detail", "text": "Returns are tracked program by program, not just overall.", "highlight": "Each category of program has a minimum return a country must receive.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "critics", "eyebrow": "The debate", "title": "Critics call it a brake", "body": "Mario Draghi's report for the EU called it a major obstacle for launch. ESA's new Launcher Challenge skips it.", "sources": [{"url": "https://europeanspaceflight.com/esa-director-general-reaffirms-geo-return-policy-as-fundamental/", "label": "European Spaceflight, geo-return reaffirmed"}]}, {"kind": "numberSense", "id": "ns-return", "prompt": "A country pays 20% of an ESA program. With a perfect return ratio of 1, what share of the contracts should its companies win, in percent?", "min": 0, "max": 50, "value": 20, "unit": "%", "explanation": "A ratio of 1 means contract share equals funding share: 20% in, 20% back."}, {"kind": "theCall", "id": "call", "situation": "You are a minister. Your country could raise its ESA pledge, but money is tight.", "prompt": "What is the strongest case for paying more?", "options": ["ESA would move its headquarters to you", "More funding brings more contracts home", "Paying more lets you skip ESA rules"], "consequences": ["ESA's headquarters do not move with pledges.", "Geo-return sends work back in proportion to what you pay.", "Every member follows the same rules."], "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "Under geo-return, a bigger pledge means more ESA work for your own companies."}, {"id": "lens-build_startup", "kind": "info", "title": "Your country's pledge is your market", "body": "ESA contracts track national funding. Check what your country pledged before you pitch ESA.", "eyebrow": "For founders", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In European space, where the money comes from decides where the work goes.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}, {"url": "https://europeanspaceflight.com/esa-director-general-reaffirms-geo-return-policy-as-fundamental/", "label": "European Spaceflight, geo-return reaffirmed"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "ESA members pledged a record €22.07 billion in November 2025. Geo-return sends contracts back to each country roughly in proportion to what it pays.", "sectionKey": "gap"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
