ity", "kind": "info", "title": "Nobody owns the Moon", "body": "Since 1967, no country can claim the Moon, and 76 countries have signed the newer Artemis Accords.", "eyebrow": "Why it matters", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.unoosa.org/documents/pdf/spacelaw/activities/2020/SLC2020Presentations/SLC2020PDFPresentations/A._Newman_-_8_Dec_2020_-_Fundamentals_of_Space_Law_.pdf", "label": "UNOOSA, fundamentals of space law"}, {"url": "https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/nasa-celebrates-as-artemis-accords-surpasses-75-signatories/", "label": "NASA, Artemis Accords pass 75 signatories"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In space, you can explore and use, but no one can claim territory.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.unoosa.org/documents/pdf/spacelaw/activities/2020/SLC2020Presentations/SLC2020PDFPresentations/A._Newman_-_8_Dec_2020_-_Fundamentals_of_Space_Law_.pdf", "label": "UNOOSA, fundamentals of space law"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "The 1967 Outer Space Treaty bars any country from claiming the Moon and makes countries answer for their companies. The Artemis Accords had 76 signatories by September 2026.", "sectionKey": "rules"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$6e62932c-ec6e-5d15-9bf9-46c8594b91d3$ml$::uuid, $ml$spacetech$ml$, $ml$The Mars rocks that may never come home$ml$, 'LESSON', ARRAY[$ml$MICRO_LESSON$ml$, $ml$day-24$ml$, $ml$month-1$ml$, $ml$handwritten-v1$ml$, $ml$goal:career$ml$, $ml$level:beginner$ml$, $ml$level:intermediate$ml$, $ml$level:advanced$ml$]::text[], 5, now(), '{}'::jsonb, $ml${"id": "spacetech-d24-career", "title": "The Mars rocks that may never come home", "exercises": [{"id": "open", "kind": "coldOpen", "kicker": "The samples are packed, but the ride home isn't funded.", "eyebrow": "Day 24 · Where it breaks", "headline": "Perseverance has collected more than 30 Mars samples, and NASA has no funded way to bring them back.", "fullText": "An independent review put Mars Sample Return at up to $11 billion, with samples not home until 2040. NASA asked industry for a cheaper, faster plan in 2024. In January 2026, Congress passed a NASA budget that does not support the existing program. China plans to launch Tianwen-3 in 2028 and return samples in 2031.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.livescience.com/space/mars/nasas-mars-sample-return-is-dead-leaving-china-to-retrieve-signs-of-life-from-the-red-planet", "label": "Live Science, Mars Sample Return cancelled"}, {"url": "https://spaceflightnow.com/2024/04/16/nasa-requests-proposals-to-reduce-cost-timeline-of-mars-sample-return-mission/", "label": "Spaceflight Now, NASA seeks cheaper Mars Sample Return"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "balloon", "eyebrow": "The cost", "text": "Estimates ballooned from $5 to $7 billion to as much as $11 billion.", "highlight": "The review projected $850 million to $1 billion a year during development.", "sources": [{"url": "https://spaceflightnow.com/2024/04/16/nasa-requests-proposals-to-reduce-cost-timeline-of-mars-sample-return-mission/", "label": "Spaceflight Now, NASA seeks cheaper Mars Sample Return"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "reset", "eyebrow": "The reset", "text": "NASA called the old plan too costly and too slow.", "highlight": "In April 2024 it asked industry and its own centers for a quicker, cheaper design.", "sources": [{"url": "https://spaceflightnow.com/2024/04/16/nasa-requests-proposals-to-reduce-cost-timeline-of-mars-sample-return-mission/", "label": "Spaceflight Now, NASA seeks cheaper Mars Sample Return"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "china", "eyebrow": "The rival", "title": "China may get there first", "body": "Tianwen-3 aims to launch in 2028 and return rocks in 2031, from an easier but less promising site.", "bullets": ["Congress kept $110 million for future Mars mission work."], "sources": [{"url": "https://www.livescience.com/space/mars/nasas-mars-sample-return-is-dead-leaving-china-to-retrieve-signs-of-life-from-the-red-planet", "label": "Live Science, Mars Sample Return cancelled"}]}, {"kind": "multipleChoice", "id": "mc", "prompt": "What sank the original Mars Sample Return plan?", "options": ["Perseverance failed to collect samples", "Its cost and schedule kept growing", "China blocked the landing site"], "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "Cost estimates rose to as much as $11 billion, with samples not back until 2040."}, {"kind": "numberSense", "id": "ns-cost", "prompt": "Mars Sample Return was estimated to cost up to how many billions of dollars?", "min": 0, "max": 25, "value": 11, "unit": "B", "explanation": "Up to $11 billion, against early estimates of $5 to $7 billion."}, {"id": "lens-career", "kind": "info", "title": "Know why big missions stall", "body": "Mars Sample Return shows how cost growth can stop a flagship. Be ready to talk about cost and schedule discipline.", "eyebrow": "For your interview", "sources": [{"url": "https://spaceflightnow.com/2024/04/16/nasa-requests-proposals-to-reduce-cost-timeline-of-mars-sample-return-mission/", "label": "Spaceflight Now, NASA seeks cheaper Mars Sample Return"}, {"url": "https://www.livescience.com/space/mars/nasas-mars-sample-return-is-dead-leaving-china-to-retrieve-signs-of-life-from-the-red-planet", "label": "Live Science, Mars Sample Return cancelled"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In space science, a mission that costs too much can stop even after the hard part is done.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://spaceflightnow.com/2024/04/16/nasa-requests-proposals-to-reduce-cost-timeline-of-mars-sample-return-mission/", "label": "Spaceflight Now, NASA seeks cheaper Mars Sample Return"}, {"url": "https://www.livescience.com/space/mars/nasas-mars-sample-return-is-dead-leaving-china-to-retrieve-signs-of-life-from-the-red-planet", "label": "Live Science, Mars Sample Return cancelled"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "Mars Sample Return grew to as much as $11 billion with a 2040 return, and in January 2026 Congress stopped supporting it. Perseverance's samples remain on Mars.", "sectionKey": "my_view"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
