and too slow.", "highlight": "In April 2024 it asked industry and its own centers for a quicker, cheaper design.", "sources": [{"url": "https://spaceflightnow.com/2024/04/16/nasa-requests-proposals-to-reduce-cost-timeline-of-mars-sample-return-mission/", "label": "Spaceflight Now, NASA seeks cheaper Mars Sample Return"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "china", "eyebrow": "The rival", "title": "China may get there first", "body": "Tianwen-3 aims to launch in 2028 and return rocks in 2031, from an easier but less promising site.", "bullets": ["Congress kept $110 million for future Mars mission work."], "sources": [{"url": "https://www.livescience.com/space/mars/nasas-mars-sample-return-is-dead-leaving-china-to-retrieve-signs-of-life-from-the-red-planet", "label": "Live Science, Mars Sample Return cancelled"}]}, {"kind": "multipleChoice", "id": "mc", "prompt": "What sank the original Mars Sample Return plan?", "options": ["Perseverance failed to collect samples", "Its cost and schedule kept growing", "China blocked the landing site"], "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "Cost estimates rose to as much as $11 billion, with samples not back until 2040."}, {"kind": "numberSense", "id": "ns-cost", "prompt": "Mars Sample Return was estimated to cost up to how many billions of dollars?", "min": 0, "max": 25, "value": 11, "unit": "B", "explanation": "Up to $11 billion, against early estimates of $5 to $7 billion."}, {"id": "lens-invest", "kind": "info", "title": "Cancellations move money", "body": "When a flagship stops, its contractors lose work and cheaper approaches get a hearing. Watch where funds go next.", "eyebrow": "For investors", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.livescience.com/space/mars/nasas-mars-sample-return-is-dead-leaving-china-to-retrieve-signs-of-life-from-the-red-planet", "label": "Live Science, Mars Sample Return cancelled"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In space science, a mission that costs too much can stop even after the hard part is done.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://spaceflightnow.com/2024/04/16/nasa-requests-proposals-to-reduce-cost-timeline-of-mars-sample-return-mission/", "label": "Spaceflight Now, NASA seeks cheaper Mars Sample Return"}, {"url": "https://www.livescience.com/space/mars/nasas-mars-sample-return-is-dead-leaving-china-to-retrieve-signs-of-life-from-the-red-planet", "label": "Live Science, Mars Sample Return cancelled"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "Mars Sample Return grew to as much as $11 billion with a 2040 return, and in January 2026 Congress stopped supporting it. Perseverance's samples remain on Mars.", "sectionKey": "review"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
