ions/A._Newman_-_8_Dec_2020_-_Fundamentals_of_Space_Law_.pdf", "label": "UNOOSA, fundamentals of space law"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In space, whoever carries the liability holds the power to say no.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.unoosa.org/documents/pdf/spacelaw/activities/2020/SLC2020Presentations/SLC2020PDFPresentations/A._Newman_-_8_Dec_2020_-_Fundamentals_of_Space_Law_.pdf", "label": "UNOOSA, fundamentals of space law"}, {"url": "https://www.unoosa.org/oosa/en/ourwork/spacelaw/nationalspacelaw/bi-multi-lateral-agreements/can_ussr_001.html", "label": "UNOOSA, Canada-USSR Cosmos 954 settlement"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "Countries are liable for damage from what they launch, as the Soviet Union was when Cosmos 954 fell on Canada. That liability is why governments control who flies.", "sectionKey": "who_hurts"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
