($ml$a2ac8843-2bcc-5622-ad57-3982d2619c04$ml$::uuid, $ml$spacetech$ml$, $ml$327,320 satellites on paper$ml$, 'LESSON', ARRAY[$ml$MICRO_LESSON$ml$, $ml$day-30$ml$, $ml$month-1$ml$, $ml$handwritten-v1$ml$, $ml$goal:career$ml$, $ml$level:beginner$ml$, $ml$level:intermediate$ml$, $ml$level:advanced$ml$]::text[], 5, now(), '{}'::jsonb, $ml${"id": "spacetech-d30-career", "title": "327,320 satellites on paper", "exercises": [{"id": "open", "kind": "coldOpen", "kicker": "Filing is easy; flying is not.", "eyebrow": "Day 30 · Where it breaks", "headline": "In September 2021, Rwanda filed at the ITU for a constellation of 327,320 satellites.", "fullText": "The filing, called CINNAMON-937, spread the satellites across 27 orbital shells. It was not clear who would build them. Filings like this reserve frequencies on paper long before anything flies, which is why the ITU added deployment milestones in 2019.", "sources": [{"url": "https://spaceinafrica.com/2021/10/14/rwanda-has-submitted-itu-filing-for-27-orbital-shells-of-327320-satellites/", "label": "Space in Africa, Rwanda's ITU filing"}, {"url": "https://itu.int/en/mediacentre/backgrounders/Pages/Non-geostationary-satellite-systems.aspx", "label": "ITU, non-geostationary satellite systems"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "scale", "eyebrow": "The scale", "text": "The filing dwarfs anything in orbit.", "highlight": "Starlink had about 9,400 active satellites in early 2026.", "sources": [{"url": "https://spaceinafrica.com/2021/10/14/rwanda-has-submitted-itu-filing-for-27-orbital-shells-of-327320-satellites/", "label": "Space in Africa, Rwanda's ITU filing"}, {"url": "https://teslanorth.com/2026/01/25/starlink-satellites-made-300000-moves-to-avoid-collisions-in-2025", "label": "TeslaNorth, citing SpaceX filing to the FCC"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "blur", "eyebrow": "The problem", "text": "Paper filings blur the picture of what will really fly.", "highlight": "The ITU's milestones aim to keep its register close to reality.", "sources": [{"url": "https://itu.int/en/mediacentre/backgrounders/Pages/Non-geostationary-satellite-systems.aspx", "label": "ITU, non-geostationary satellite systems"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "gap", "eyebrow": "The gap", "title": "Telling real from paper", "body": "Regulators, investors and operators all need better ways to judge which filings will actually launch.", "bullets": ["A subset, CINNAMON-217, alone covered 52,080 satellites."], "sources": [{"url": "https://spaceinafrica.com/2021/10/14/rwanda-has-submitted-itu-filing-for-27-orbital-shells-of-327320-satellites/", "label": "Space in Africa, Rwanda's ITU filing"}, {"url": "https://itu.int/en/mediacentre/backgrounders/Pages/Non-geostationary-satellite-systems.aspx", "label": "ITU, non-geostationary satellite systems"}]}, {"kind": "numberSense", "id": "ns-ratio", "prompt": "Rwanda's filing covered 327,320 satellites; Starlink had about 9,400. Roughly how many times larger was the filing?", "min": 0, "max": 100, "value": 35, "unit": "x", "explanation": "About 35 times Starlink's active fleet."}, {"kind": "multipleChoice", "id": "mc", "prompt": "Why did the ITU add deployment milestones in 2019?", "options": ["To keep filings close to what actually flies", "To raise more money from ITU filing fees", "To ban any constellation over 1,000 satellites"], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "The milestones aim to make the register reflect real deployment and to prevent spectrum warehousing."}, {"id": "lens-career", "kind": "info", "title": "Separate filings from fleets", "body": "A filing is not a satellite. Ask how many are actually in orbit before you judge a constellation.", "eyebrow": "For your interview", "sources": [{"url": "https://spaceinafrica.com/2021/10/14/rwanda-has-submitted-itu-filing-for-27-orbital-shells-of-327320-satellites/", "label": "Space in Africa, Rwanda's ITU filing"}, {"url": "https://teslanorth.com/2026/01/25/starlink-satellites-made-300000-moves-to-avoid-collisions-in-2025", "label": "TeslaNorth, citing SpaceX filing to the FCC"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In space, a filing reserves a claim, but only launches make it real.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://itu.int/en/mediacentre/backgrounders/Pages/Non-geostationary-satellite-systems.aspx", "label": "ITU, non-geostationary satellite systems"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "Rwanda filed for 327,320 satellites in 2021, about 35 times Starlink's fleet. Paper filings are why the ITU now requires deployment milestones.", "sectionKey": "my_view"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
