($ml$c444a1e8-51fb-58a8-b147-4aec096b4b41$ml$::uuid, $ml$b88521b1-8e01-5d33-8dfe-e7ff30a1c7da$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 11 · The risk$ml$, $ml$In February 2022, a geomagnetic storm brought down 38 of 49 new Starlink satellites. SpaceX launched 49 Starlink satellites on February 3, 2022. Solar plasma from a geomagnetic storm heated the upper atmosphere, and denser gas expanded into the satellites' orbit. Drag rose, and 38 of them reentered and burned up within days. Forecasters had expected only minor storming.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/hyperwall/index/data/a000000/a005100/a005193/cap5193.txt.html", "label": "NASA, geomagnetic storm causes Starlink loss"}, {"url": "https://cires.colorado.edu/news/minor-geomagnetic-storm-big-impact-february-2022-starlink-satellite-loss", "label": "CIRES, minor storm, big impact"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$eb951d52-13b6-5d1b-a8d2-97a04875954c$ml$::uuid, $ml$b88521b1-8e01-5d33-8dfe-e7ff30a1c7da$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The physics$ml$, $ml$Low orbit is not empty: thin air still drags on satellites. When the Sun heats it, that air swells upward and drag rises.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/hyperwall/index/data/a000000/a005100/a005193/cap5193.txt.html", "label": "NASA, geomagnetic storm causes Starlink loss"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$6df6e31b-6096-5da2-bb44-7da1ecbca274$ml$::uuid, $ml$b88521b1-8e01-5d33-8dfe-e7ff30a1c7da$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The surprise$ml$, $ml$The forecast called it minor. A small storm was enough to wipe out most of a launch.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://cires.colorado.edu/news/minor-geomagnetic-storm-big-impact-february-2022-starlink-satellite-loss", "label": "CIRES, minor storm, big impact"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$94493311-beba-5cb0-bcc9-0ae9029d3227$ml$::uuid, $ml$b88521b1-8e01-5d33-8dfe-e7ff30a1c7da$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Drag cuts both ways$ml$, $ml$It pulls dead satellites down, which keeps low orbit cleaner. It also pulls down working ones that cannot push back.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/hyperwall/index/data/a000000/a005100/a005193/cap5193.txt.html", "label": "NASA, geomagnetic storm causes Starlink loss"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$2a590132-87bb-52c4-914f-f372965a828b$ml$::uuid, $ml$b88521b1-8e01-5d33-8dfe-e7ff30a1c7da$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Space weather is an ops topic$ml$, $ml$Since 2022, space weather is part of planning any low-orbit launch. Explaining why shows you think like an operator.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/hyperwall/index/data/a000000/a005100/a005193/cap5193.txt.html", "label": "NASA, geomagnetic storm causes Starlink loss"}, {"url": "https://cires.colorado.edu/news/minor-geomagnetic-storm-big-impact-february-2022-starlink-satellite-loss", "label": "CIRES, minor storm, big impact"}]$ml$::jsonb),
