($ml$a264ae78-7f3a-55f4-96b7-524c404c5302$ml$::uuid, $ml$31730f0a-338e-5b8c-9eff-1cc720558587$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 12 · Where it breaks$ml$, $ml$Starlink satellites made about 300,000 collision-avoidance maneuvers in 2025. SpaceX told the FCC its satellites dodged roughly 300,000 possible collisions in 2025, nearly 40 per satellite. In the six months to May 2023 the count was about 25,000. SpaceX moves when collision risk reaches about three in ten million, far more cautious than the common one-in-10,000 threshold.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://teslanorth.com/2026/01/25/starlink-satellites-made-300000-moves-to-avoid-collisions-in-2025", "label": "TeslaNorth, citing SpaceX filing to the FCC"}, {"url": "https://space.com/spacex-starlink-50000-collision-avoidance-maneuvers-space-safety", "label": "Space.com, 50,000 maneuvers in six months"}]$ml$::jsonb),
