($ml$30548d3d-24d6-58b9-b7fe-5120a1d289f7$ml$::uuid, $ml$e228533e-5aa9-5bd8-8697-c2dd96334cf6$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 16 · The numbers$ml$, $ml$In the third quarter of 2024, SpaceX carried 85.7% of all mass launched to space. SpaceX launched 362 metric tons of payload in those three months. Counting launches undersells how concentrated the market is: a few heavy, frequent rockets carry most of the mass. In 2025 Falcon 9 flew about once every 2.2 days.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.newsminimalist.com/articles/spacex-launches-86percent-of-global-payload-to-space-in-third-quarter-of-2024-452b896c", "label": "SpaceX share of global upmass, Q3 2024"}, {"url": "https://spacedaily.com/t-we-tend-to-think-reusable-rockets-are-still-experimental-but-in-2025-spacex-s-partly-reusable-falcon-9-flew-165-missions-one-every-2-2-days-and-successfully-delivered-its-payload-on-every-flight/", "label": "Space Daily, Falcon 9 in 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$59f54c12-8d8a-5f6a-a531-e4e379b8231b$ml$::uuid, $ml$e228533e-5aa9-5bd8-8697-c2dd96334cf6$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The metric$ml$, $ml$Upmass is the total weight a company sends to orbit. It shows who really carries the market.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.newsminimalist.com/articles/spacex-launches-86percent-of-global-payload-to-space-in-third-quarter-of-2024-452b896c", "label": "SpaceX share of global upmass, Q3 2024"}]$ml$::jsonb),
