($ml$97e7b803-5f55-5e87-ad5f-553e778228a3$ml$::uuid, $ml$f37a03aa-25de-5e6b-988f-b8ef525ef65e$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 17 · The rule$ml$, $ml$On July 11, 2024, a Falcon 9 upper stage failed and 20 Starlink satellites were lost. An oxygen leak developed when the second-stage engine fired a second time, leaving the satellites too low to survive. No one on the ground was hurt, but the FAA required an investigation before Falcon 9 could fly again. It was only the rocket's second in-flight failure, after 364 successful flights since 2010.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://spacepolicyonline.com/news/rare-spacex-failure-leaves-launch-schedules-in-flux/", "label": "SpacePolicyOnline, rare SpaceX failure"}]$ml$::jsonb),
