($ml$df3000aa-c980-50da-a522-16c1e6a0af7b$ml$::uuid, $ml$1c5b6184-cfce-531e-9280-eb94c14081ba$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 17 · The rule$ml$, $ml$On July 11, 2024, a Falcon 9 upper stage failed and 20 Starlink satellites were lost. An oxygen leak developed when the second-stage engine fired a second time, leaving the satellites too low to survive. No one on the ground was hurt, but the FAA required an investigation before Falcon 9 could fly again. It was only the rocket's second in-flight failure, after 364 successful flights since 2010.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://spacepolicyonline.com/news/rare-spacex-failure-leaves-launch-schedules-in-flux/", "label": "SpacePolicyOnline, rare SpaceX failure"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$77554af0-40db-521a-a928-b8ae5105b3ae$ml$::uuid, $ml$1c5b6184-cfce-531e-9280-eb94c14081ba$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$Who decides$ml$, $ml$After a mishap, the FAA must be satisfied that public safety is not at risk. Until then, the rocket stays on the ground.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://spacepolicyonline.com/news/rare-spacex-failure-leaves-launch-schedules-in-flux/", "label": "SpacePolicyOnline, rare SpaceX failure"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$8176005e-82c4-57f9-b976-39c987fbe6d8$ml$::uuid, $ml$1c5b6184-cfce-531e-9280-eb94c14081ba$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The cause$ml$, $ml$A cracked oxygen sense line, worn by engine vibration, caused the leak. Crewed flights and NASA science missions were waiting behind it.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://cosmiclog.com/2024/07/27/spacex-resumes-falcon-9-launches-after-faa-go-ahead/", "label": "Cosmic Log, Falcon 9 returns after FAA go-ahead"}, {"url": "https://spacepolicyonline.com/news/rare-spacex-failure-leaves-launch-schedules-in-flux/", "label": "SpacePolicyOnline, rare SpaceX failure"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$04439f9c-dd6e-5fbb-8c37-a1201a784b06$ml$::uuid, $ml$1c5b6184-cfce-531e-9280-eb94c14081ba$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Back in 16 days$ml$, $ml$The FAA allowed Falcon 9 to return to flight on July 25, 2024, and it launched again on July 27.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://cosmiclog.com/2024/07/27/spacex-resumes-falcon-9-launches-after-faa-go-ahead/", "label": "Cosmic Log, Falcon 9 returns after FAA go-ahead"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$41ffc7d0-4118-5718-9f19-987c55a5932e$ml$::uuid, $ml$1c5b6184-cfce-531e-9280-eb94c14081ba$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$364 successes, then a stop$ml$, $ml$Falcon 9 had flown 364 times successfully before the July 2024 failure grounded it.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://spacepolicyonline.com/news/rare-spacex-failure-leaves-launch-schedules-in-flux/", "label": "SpacePolicyOnline, rare SpaceX failure"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$ffafffc9-567e-54fa-8da4-7cdc6530f1be$ml$::uuid, $ml$1c5b6184-cfce-531e-9280-eb94c14081ba$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In launch, safety rules can stop even the most reliable rocket.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://spacepolicyonline.com/news/rare-spacex-failure-leaves-launch-schedules-in-flux/", "label": "SpacePolicyOnline, rare SpaceX failure"}, {"url": "https://cosmiclog.com/2024/07/27/spacex-resumes-falcon-9-launches-after-faa-go-ahead/", "label": "Cosmic Log, Falcon 9 returns after FAA go-ahead"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$d7d75dcf-76c4-58aa-988e-d8ec579fd5db$ml$::uuid, $ml$cbbcb0a6-41b4-506a-8a5c-ab3ab5ce6bf6$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 18 · Where it breaks$ml$, $ml$Virgin Orbit filed for bankruptcy in April 2023, three months after a failed launch from the UK. Virgin Orbit dropped small rockets from under the wing of a Boeing 747. Investors put in more than $1 billion, but it flew only six times and lost $191.1 million in 2022. After the January 2023 failure, the first orbital attempt from UK soil, it laid off all but 100 of its nearly 800 staff and filed for Chapter 11.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://thespacereview.com/article/4593/1", "label": "The Space Review, death of a launch company"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$3c84871a-49ca-5400-a6df-22824bc89590$ml$::uuid, $ml$cbbcb0a6-41b4-506a-8a5c-ab3ab5ce6bf6$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The math$ml$, $ml$Small launchers face hard math: few flights, high fixed costs. Virgin Orbit lost about $50 million a quarter.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://thespacereview.com/article/4593/1", "label": "The Space Review, death of a launch company"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$5acd2970-cee3-5651-9de0-0f0b226adb54$ml$::uuid, $ml$cbbcb0a6-41b4-506a-8a5c-ab3ab5ce6bf6$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The end$ml$, $ml$Its assets sold for about $36.5 million at auction. Rocket Lab paid $16.1 million for its factory; Stratolaunch $17 million for the 747.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://thespacereview.com/article/4593/1", "label": "The Space Review, death of a launch company"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$373c3b68-5939-5a1a-8ff7-0218cafe86c1$ml$::uuid, $ml$cbbcb0a6-41b4-506a-8a5c-ab3ab5ce6bf6$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Cheap rideshare squeezes small rockets$ml$, $ml$Small satellites can share a big rocket at about $7,000 per kg. A dedicated small launch has to win on timing and orbit.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://newspaceeconomy.ca/2026/02/27/satellite-ridesharing-market-analysis-2026/", "label": "New Space Economy, rideshare market 2026"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$7c533e2f-a5e2-50f3-9976-3aee381ac17e$ml$::uuid, $ml$cbbcb0a6-41b4-506a-8a5c-ab3ab5ce6bf6$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Ask how a launcher breaks even$ml$, $ml$Ask how many flights a year a launch company needs to cover its costs. It is the question that sank Virgin Orbit.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://thespacereview.com/article/4593/1", "label": "The Space Review, death of a launch company"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$391bd84b-5730-5e72-a49a-28c3fcb663c4$ml$::uuid, $ml$cbbcb0a6-41b4-506a-8a5c-ab3ab5ce6bf6$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In launch, flying too rarely can sink even a well-funded company.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://thespacereview.com/article/4593/1", "label": "The Space Review, death of a launch company"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$787663ef-f7ff-5892-aed5-181fe2bd3dce$ml$::uuid, $ml$429a538f-38bc-567a-834e-2ed1e14de6b6$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 18 · Where it breaks$ml$, $ml$Virgin Orbit filed for bankruptcy in April 2023, three months after a failed launch from the UK. Virgin Orbit dropped small rockets from under the wing of a Boeing 747. Investors put in more than $1 billion, but it flew only six times and lost $191.1 million in 2022. After the January 2023 failure, the first orbital attempt from UK soil, it laid off all but 100 of its nearly 800 staff and filed for Chapter 11.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://thespacereview.com/article/4593/1", "label": "The Space Review, death of a launch company"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$cc841175-6f9d-52ef-94ea-98dac22fed21$ml$::uuid, $ml$429a538f-38bc-567a-834e-2ed1e14de6b6$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The math$ml$, $ml$Small launchers face hard math: few flights, high fixed costs. Virgin Orbit lost about $50 million a quarter.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://thespacereview.com/article/4593/1", "label": "The Space Review, death of a launch company"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$4cf70b1b-ea66-5be6-8dc8-c8253e506d2d$ml$::uuid, $ml$429a538f-38bc-567a-834e-2ed1e14de6b6$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The end$ml$, $ml$Its assets sold for about $36.5 million at auction. Rocket Lab paid $16.1 million for its factory; Stratolaunch $17 million for the 747.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://thespacereview.com/article/4593/1", "label": "The Space Review, death of a launch company"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$e47323d3-fa9a-53d6-aa22-60c4c4053ef5$ml$::uuid, $ml$429a538f-38bc-567a-834e-2ed1e14de6b6$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Cheap rideshare squeezes small rockets$ml$, $ml$Small satellites can share a big rocket at about $7,000 per kg. A dedicated small launch has to win on timing and orbit.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://newspaceeconomy.ca/2026/02/27/satellite-ridesharing-market-analysis-2026/", "label": "New Space Economy, rideshare market 2026"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$2a0b343f-1922-579a-b112-c5493a53bd41$ml$::uuid, $ml$429a538f-38bc-567a-834e-2ed1e14de6b6$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Cadence decides survival$ml$, $ml$Six launches could not support more than $1 billion of investment. Check flight rate before backing a launcher.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://thespacereview.com/article/4593/1", "label": "The Space Review, death of a launch company"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$88a1997c-866a-5d5e-b20c-4e8d87699f17$ml$::uuid, $ml$429a538f-38bc-567a-834e-2ed1e14de6b6$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In launch, flying too rarely can sink even a well-funded company.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://thespacereview.com/article/4593/1", "label": "The Space Review, death of a launch company"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$326a326d-36dc-51ea-a345-ef2a43d7dab5$ml$::uuid, $ml$ac83fd9e-a20f-5982-a7dd-238796834d51$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 18 · Where it breaks$ml$, $ml$Virgin Orbit filed for bankruptcy in April 2023, three months after a failed launch from the UK. Virgin Orbit dropped small rockets from under the wing of a Boeing 747. Investors put in more than $1 billion, but it flew only six times and lost $191.1 million in 2022. After the January 2023 failure, the first orbital attempt from UK soil, it laid off all but 100 of its nearly 800 staff and filed for Chapter 11.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://thespacereview.com/article/4593/1", "label": "The Space Review, death of a launch company"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$85fb838b-2b90-5794-8b46-eba55658c9bb$ml$::uuid, $ml$ac83fd9e-a20f-5982-a7dd-238796834d51$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The math$ml$, $ml$Small launchers face hard math: few flights, high fixed costs. Virgin Orbit lost about $50 million a quarter.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://thespacereview.com/article/4593/1", "label": "The Space Review, death of a launch company"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$f99e04e9-6e83-5ba7-9195-4c75c4b03936$ml$::uuid, $ml$ac83fd9e-a20f-5982-a7dd-238796834d51$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The end$ml$, $ml$Its assets sold for about $36.5 million at auction. Rocket Lab paid $16.1 million for its factory; Stratolaunch $17 million for the 747.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://thespacereview.com/article/4593/1", "label": "The Space Review, death of a launch company"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$105ab076-fa08-5e84-9941-d16db0220d4b$ml$::uuid, $ml$ac83fd9e-a20f-5982-a7dd-238796834d51$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Cheap rideshare squeezes small rockets$ml$, $ml$Small satellites can share a big rocket at about $7,000 per kg. A dedicated small launch has to win on timing and orbit.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://newspaceeconomy.ca/2026/02/27/satellite-ridesharing-market-analysis-2026/", "label": "New Space Economy, rideshare market 2026"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$ef8748b0-0a07-5a2a-9f21-0cf1399f24b2$ml$::uuid, $ml$ac83fd9e-a20f-5982-a7dd-238796834d51$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Price against rideshare$ml$, $ml$A small launcher competes with rideshare at about $7,000 per kg. Sell what rideshare can't: your orbit, your date.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://newspaceeconomy.ca/2026/02/27/satellite-ridesharing-market-analysis-2026/", "label": "New Space Economy, rideshare market 2026"}, {"url": "https://thespacereview.com/article/4593/1", "label": "The Space Review, death of a launch company"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$7e2251d4-6587-566f-b02d-9c1a0dc13eb2$ml$::uuid, $ml$ac83fd9e-a20f-5982-a7dd-238796834d51$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In launch, flying too rarely can sink even a well-funded company.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://thespacereview.com/article/4593/1", "label": "The Space Review, death of a launch company"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$3c6dfecc-336f-56a3-9a94-bdb0d2af95a6$ml$::uuid, $ml$f89019ed-5418-5d63-a6a4-a9634a103b40$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 18 · Where it breaks$ml$, $ml$Virgin Orbit filed for bankruptcy in April 2023, three months after a failed launch from the UK. Virgin Orbit dropped small rockets from under the wing of a Boeing 747. Investors put in more than $1 billion, but it flew only six times and lost $191.1 million in 2022. After the January 2023 failure, the first orbital attempt from UK soil, it laid off all but 100 of its nearly 800 staff and filed for Chapter 11.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://thespacereview.com/article/4593/1", "label": "The Space Review, death of a launch company"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$cd26a702-d22c-5559-9cc4-78d621772d8a$ml$::uuid, $ml$f89019ed-5418-5d63-a6a4-a9634a103b40$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The math$ml$, $ml$Small launchers face hard math: few flights, high fixed costs. Virgin Orbit lost about $50 million a quarter.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://thespacereview.com/article/4593/1", "label": "The Space Review, death of a launch company"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$dd3d7508-9136-5b58-9425-59691a1bf615$ml$::uuid, $ml$f89019ed-5418-5d63-a6a4-a9634a103b40$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The end$ml$, $ml$Its assets sold for about $36.5 million at auction. Rocket Lab paid $16.1 million for its factory; Stratolaunch $17 million for the 747.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://thespacereview.com/article/4593/1", "label": "The Space Review, death of a launch company"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$1c5858f7-a20d-5e87-b82f-ae3f0442480d$ml$::uuid, $ml$f89019ed-5418-5d63-a6a4-a9634a103b40$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Cheap rideshare squeezes small rockets$ml$, $ml$Small satellites can share a big rocket at about $7,000 per kg. A dedicated small launch has to win on timing and orbit.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://newspaceeconomy.ca/2026/02/27/satellite-ridesharing-market-analysis-2026/", "label": "New Space Economy, rideshare market 2026"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$676858a7-92a2-52b6-aa82-9dcb4eb88ced$ml$::uuid, $ml$f89019ed-5418-5d63-a6a4-a9634a103b40$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$A rocket from a jumbo jet$ml$, $ml$Virgin Orbit dropped its rockets from a Boeing 747. The jet later sold at auction for $17 million.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://thespacereview.com/article/4593/1", "label": "The Space Review, death of a launch company"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$7d33fb4e-79d5-52ef-8308-50d1d6a0cb54$ml$::uuid, $ml$f89019ed-5418-5d63-a6a4-a9634a103b40$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In launch, flying too rarely can sink even a well-funded company.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://thespacereview.com/article/4593/1", "label": "The Space Review, death of a launch company"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$2c1a42a5-f632-5188-9cee-b13bd61b4357$ml$::uuid, $ml$7ecef5c7-ed6d-5fd9-bd68-0bbb4416e1dd$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 19 · Agencies$ml$, $ml$ESA's 2025 budget was €7.7 billion, with €4.8 billion from its member states. The European Union added €1.7 billion and other sources €1.2 billion. ESA spends it as a customer, placing contracts with companies across its member states. NASA works the same way at a larger scale: Congress passed $24.4 billion for it in fiscal 2026.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://aviationweek.com/space/budget-policy-regulation/esa-council-oks-initial-eu77b-2025-budget-readies-launcher-challenge", "label": "Aviation Week, ESA 2025 budget"}, {"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}, {"url": "https://space.com/space-exploration/in-rejection-of-trumps-deep-cuts-congress-passes-usd24-4-billion-budget-for-nasa", "label": "Space.com, NASA fiscal 2026 budget"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$706cdca2-5bb2-51d2-8bf2-e3fe832e1a64$ml$::uuid, $ml$7ecef5c7-ed6d-5fd9-bd68-0bbb4416e1dd$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The role$ml$, $ml$A space agency is mostly a customer: it pays companies to build what it plans. ESA describes itself as an intergovernmental customer.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$1c54ad55-8bdc-52ba-a11e-c793cef5feb6$ml$::uuid, $ml$7ecef5c7-ed6d-5fd9-bd68-0bbb4416e1dd$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The scale$ml$, $ml$NASA's budget is about three times ESA's. $24.4 billion for fiscal 2026, against €7.7 billion for ESA in 2025.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://space.com/space-exploration/in-rejection-of-trumps-deep-cuts-congress-passes-usd24-4-billion-budget-for-nasa", "label": "Space.com, NASA fiscal 2026 budget"}, {"url": "https://aviationweek.com/space/budget-policy-regulation/esa-council-oks-initial-eu77b-2025-budget-readies-launcher-challenge", "label": "Aviation Week, ESA 2025 budget"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$f25b7aa5-9870-571b-b580-53b6c894f753$ml$::uuid, $ml$7ecef5c7-ed6d-5fd9-bd68-0bbb4416e1dd$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Agency plans become industry work$ml$, $ml$When an agency starts a program, the money turns into multi-year contracts for companies. Member states provided €4.8 billion of ESA's 2025 budget.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}, {"url": "https://aviationweek.com/space/budget-policy-regulation/esa-council-oks-initial-eu77b-2025-budget-readies-launcher-challenge", "label": "Aviation Week, ESA 2025 budget"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$31c7a2a2-1005-509f-a96b-268aef50cabd$ml$::uuid, $ml$7ecef5c7-ed6d-5fd9-bd68-0bbb4416e1dd$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Follow the agency contracts$ml$, $ml$Many space jobs exist because an agency funded a program. Ask which agency contract a team works under.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$5dbf5721-5979-556a-9d25-a1dca4b3cdb8$ml$::uuid, $ml$7ecef5c7-ed6d-5fd9-bd68-0bbb4416e1dd$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In space, agencies set the plans and industry builds them.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$12c51afe-e232-58c4-845d-4d20ecb26140$ml$::uuid, $ml$38a29961-6c94-5ad1-8faf-b7b870b3eddf$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 19 · Agencies$ml$, $ml$ESA's 2025 budget was €7.7 billion, with €4.8 billion from its member states. The European Union added €1.7 billion and other sources €1.2 billion. ESA spends it as a customer, placing contracts with companies across its member states. NASA works the same way at a larger scale: Congress passed $24.4 billion for it in fiscal 2026.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://aviationweek.com/space/budget-policy-regulation/esa-council-oks-initial-eu77b-2025-budget-readies-launcher-challenge", "label": "Aviation Week, ESA 2025 budget"}, {"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}, {"url": "https://space.com/space-exploration/in-rejection-of-trumps-deep-cuts-congress-passes-usd24-4-billion-budget-for-nasa", "label": "Space.com, NASA fiscal 2026 budget"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$1ca0091b-ceab-5898-bc22-5a2861373638$ml$::uuid, $ml$38a29961-6c94-5ad1-8faf-b7b870b3eddf$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The role$ml$, $ml$A space agency is mostly a customer: it pays companies to build what it plans. ESA describes itself as an intergovernmental customer.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$777cdca7-2cd0-50fd-a470-fe39bf850639$ml$::uuid, $ml$38a29961-6c94-5ad1-8faf-b7b870b3eddf$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The scale$ml$, $ml$NASA's budget is about three times ESA's. $24.4 billion for fiscal 2026, against €7.7 billion for ESA in 2025.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://space.com/space-exploration/in-rejection-of-trumps-deep-cuts-congress-passes-usd24-4-billion-budget-for-nasa", "label": "Space.com, NASA fiscal 2026 budget"}, {"url": "https://aviationweek.com/space/budget-policy-regulation/esa-council-oks-initial-eu77b-2025-budget-readies-launcher-challenge", "label": "Aviation Week, ESA 2025 budget"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$94dcdb98-a457-5ed9-9b9b-56dae81baddd$ml$::uuid, $ml$38a29961-6c94-5ad1-8faf-b7b870b3eddf$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Agency plans become industry work$ml$, $ml$When an agency starts a program, the money turns into multi-year contracts for companies. Member states provided €4.8 billion of ESA's 2025 budget.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}, {"url": "https://aviationweek.com/space/budget-policy-regulation/esa-council-oks-initial-eu77b-2025-budget-readies-launcher-challenge", "label": "Aviation Week, ESA 2025 budget"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$38209fba-c336-5b3a-9aca-47027a85ce78$ml$::uuid, $ml$38a29961-6c94-5ad1-8faf-b7b870b3eddf$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Agency budgets drive revenue$ml$, $ml$Agencies spend much of their budgets with industry. Budget decisions show up in contractors' order books.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}, {"url": "https://space.com/space-exploration/in-rejection-of-trumps-deep-cuts-congress-passes-usd24-4-billion-budget-for-nasa", "label": "Space.com, NASA fiscal 2026 budget"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$c2fa03eb-f285-5136-9363-aa1609276b4e$ml$::uuid, $ml$38a29961-6c94-5ad1-8faf-b7b870b3eddf$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In space, agencies set the plans and industry builds them.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$c4fea19e-06a0-54f7-8592-55b7dad01ea0$ml$::uuid, $ml$461e6178-ba78-5e7c-a1a9-60b6b3909d7c$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 19 · Agencies$ml$, $ml$ESA's 2025 budget was €7.7 billion, with €4.8 billion from its member states. The European Union added €1.7 billion and other sources €1.2 billion. ESA spends it as a customer, placing contracts with companies across its member states. NASA works the same way at a larger scale: Congress passed $24.4 billion for it in fiscal 2026.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://aviationweek.com/space/budget-policy-regulation/esa-council-oks-initial-eu77b-2025-budget-readies-launcher-challenge", "label": "Aviation Week, ESA 2025 budget"}, {"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}, {"url": "https://space.com/space-exploration/in-rejection-of-trumps-deep-cuts-congress-passes-usd24-4-billion-budget-for-nasa", "label": "Space.com, NASA fiscal 2026 budget"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$1d3667d6-58d5-5ff3-8bdb-0e79cc0d08d2$ml$::uuid, $ml$461e6178-ba78-5e7c-a1a9-60b6b3909d7c$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The role$ml$, $ml$A space agency is mostly a customer: it pays companies to build what it plans. ESA describes itself as an intergovernmental customer.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$7444dea8-7bdf-5b98-9533-741320a3f600$ml$::uuid, $ml$461e6178-ba78-5e7c-a1a9-60b6b3909d7c$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The scale$ml$, $ml$NASA's budget is about three times ESA's. $24.4 billion for fiscal 2026, against €7.7 billion for ESA in 2025.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://space.com/space-exploration/in-rejection-of-trumps-deep-cuts-congress-passes-usd24-4-billion-budget-for-nasa", "label": "Space.com, NASA fiscal 2026 budget"}, {"url": "https://aviationweek.com/space/budget-policy-regulation/esa-council-oks-initial-eu77b-2025-budget-readies-launcher-challenge", "label": "Aviation Week, ESA 2025 budget"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$1979c67c-b485-5f70-b347-343e9ab53484$ml$::uuid, $ml$461e6178-ba78-5e7c-a1a9-60b6b3909d7c$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Agency plans become industry work$ml$, $ml$When an agency starts a program, the money turns into multi-year contracts for companies. Member states provided €4.8 billion of ESA's 2025 budget.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}, {"url": "https://aviationweek.com/space/budget-policy-regulation/esa-council-oks-initial-eu77b-2025-budget-readies-launcher-challenge", "label": "Aviation Week, ESA 2025 budget"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$bafb6b9d-5152-5f03-803f-c4a632a99b3d$ml$::uuid, $ml$461e6178-ba78-5e7c-a1a9-60b6b3909d7c$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$An agency can be a first customer$ml$, $ml$Agencies buy studies, technology and services from companies. A small contract can prove your idea.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$d68c2b76-d325-5f79-b372-665341dd11a6$ml$::uuid, $ml$461e6178-ba78-5e7c-a1a9-60b6b3909d7c$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In space, agencies set the plans and industry builds them.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$06f8f602-551f-5907-b615-8404973f3652$ml$::uuid, $ml$160ce5a6-c4ac-566f-b3ee-c0bbd486225c$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 19 · Agencies$ml$, $ml$ESA's 2025 budget was €7.7 billion, with €4.8 billion from its member states. The European Union added €1.7 billion and other sources €1.2 billion. ESA spends it as a customer, placing contracts with companies across its member states. NASA works the same way at a larger scale: Congress passed $24.4 billion for it in fiscal 2026.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://aviationweek.com/space/budget-policy-regulation/esa-council-oks-initial-eu77b-2025-budget-readies-launcher-challenge", "label": "Aviation Week, ESA 2025 budget"}, {"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}, {"url": "https://space.com/space-exploration/in-rejection-of-trumps-deep-cuts-congress-passes-usd24-4-billion-budget-for-nasa", "label": "Space.com, NASA fiscal 2026 budget"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$51fe3cde-7e88-5e0d-b5ee-21ebf2ca674d$ml$::uuid, $ml$160ce5a6-c4ac-566f-b3ee-c0bbd486225c$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The role$ml$, $ml$A space agency is mostly a customer: it pays companies to build what it plans. ESA describes itself as an intergovernmental customer.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$4f7aee8b-038b-538d-95e2-1476cc0afab2$ml$::uuid, $ml$160ce5a6-c4ac-566f-b3ee-c0bbd486225c$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The scale$ml$, $ml$NASA's budget is about three times ESA's. $24.4 billion for fiscal 2026, against €7.7 billion for ESA in 2025.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://space.com/space-exploration/in-rejection-of-trumps-deep-cuts-congress-passes-usd24-4-billion-budget-for-nasa", "label": "Space.com, NASA fiscal 2026 budget"}, {"url": "https://aviationweek.com/space/budget-policy-regulation/esa-council-oks-initial-eu77b-2025-budget-readies-launcher-challenge", "label": "Aviation Week, ESA 2025 budget"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$b2637926-bc2d-527e-a975-dde62b45ca50$ml$::uuid, $ml$160ce5a6-c4ac-566f-b3ee-c0bbd486225c$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Agency plans become industry work$ml$, $ml$When an agency starts a program, the money turns into multi-year contracts for companies. Member states provided €4.8 billion of ESA's 2025 budget.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}, {"url": "https://aviationweek.com/space/budget-policy-regulation/esa-council-oks-initial-eu77b-2025-budget-readies-launcher-challenge", "label": "Aviation Week, ESA 2025 budget"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$eb3d7388-b9c6-5271-9013-7927b8f3bfd0$ml$::uuid, $ml$160ce5a6-c4ac-566f-b3ee-c0bbd486225c$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Who pays for exploration$ml$, $ml$Most missions you hear about are paid for by an agency but built by companies under contract.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$b79ae517-8d2b-5015-b741-afc195505873$ml$::uuid, $ml$160ce5a6-c4ac-566f-b3ee-c0bbd486225c$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In space, agencies set the plans and industry builds them.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$bc947aab-d600-5f63-b512-83fa93181c02$ml$::uuid, $ml$bbed2c94-b1cb-5e16-90f2-4a03e2d0be1e$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 20 · The money$ml$, $ml$In November 2025, ESA's members pledged a record €22.07 billion for the next three years. That was 32% more than in 2022, or 17% after inflation. Under ESA's geographical return rule, contracts flow back to each country's industry roughly in proportion to what it pays in. The rule gives countries a reason to contribute, but critics say it adds cost and slows programs.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://spacepolicyonline.com/?p=85281", "label": "SpacePolicyOnline, ESA members pledge record funding"}, {"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}, {"url": "https://europeanspaceflight.com/esa-director-general-reaffirms-geo-return-policy-as-fundamental/", "label": "European Spaceflight, geo-return reaffirmed"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$06b8cbc0-c45b-5577-a2f9-ac690bc49659$ml$::uuid, $ml$bbed2c94-b1cb-5e16-90f2-4a03e2d0be1e$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$Geo-return aims for a ratio of 1: a country's share of contracts matches its share of funding. In practice, ratios run between 0.9 and 0.95 over five years.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}, {"url": "https://europeanspaceflight.com/esa-director-general-reaffirms-geo-return-policy-as-fundamental/", "label": "European Spaceflight, geo-return reaffirmed"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$b35039ed-7823-5edc-95db-5c77dc6426aa$ml$::uuid, $ml$bbed2c94-b1cb-5e16-90f2-4a03e2d0be1e$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The detail$ml$, $ml$Returns are tracked program by program, not just overall. Each category of program has a minimum return a country must receive.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$a713efb7-4118-5290-b87a-d132a9852a84$ml$::uuid, $ml$bbed2c94-b1cb-5e16-90f2-4a03e2d0be1e$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Critics call it a brake$ml$, $ml$Mario Draghi's report for the EU called it a major obstacle for launch. ESA's new Launcher Challenge skips it.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://europeanspaceflight.com/esa-director-general-reaffirms-geo-return-policy-as-fundamental/", "label": "European Spaceflight, geo-return reaffirmed"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$29df4bf1-be4f-55b9-91a5-9dd010c9e9ba$ml$::uuid, $ml$bbed2c94-b1cb-5e16-90f2-4a03e2d0be1e$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Know where the work lands$ml$, $ml$In Europe, where a project is built depends on who paid for it. That shapes where space jobs are.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$12914eec-b80d-5a1f-8e5b-bb6078b4eba3$ml$::uuid, $ml$bbed2c94-b1cb-5e16-90f2-4a03e2d0be1e$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In European space, where the money comes from decides where the work goes.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.esa.int/About_Us/Business_with_ESA/Business_Opportunities/ESA_an_intergovernmental_customer", "label": "ESA, an intergovernmental customer"}, {"url": "https://europeanspaceflight.com/esa-director-general-reaffirms-geo-return-policy-as-fundamental/", "label": "European Spaceflight, geo-return reaffirmed"}]$ml$::jsonb),
