($ml$b2a8a99d-0e97-5131-b1ba-f52e1821b621$ml$::uuid, $ml$a1675ea8-941f-52b0-a637-9cc387c494e4$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In space science, a mission that costs too much can stop even after the hard part is done.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://spaceflightnow.com/2024/04/16/nasa-requests-proposals-to-reduce-cost-timeline-of-mars-sample-return-mission/", "label": "Spaceflight Now, NASA seeks cheaper Mars Sample Return"}, {"url": "https://www.livescience.com/space/mars/nasas-mars-sample-return-is-dead-leaving-china-to-retrieve-signs-of-life-from-the-red-planet", "label": "Live Science, Mars Sample Return cancelled"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$82993b22-c374-5e8b-a4ad-d34930a49405$ml$::uuid, $ml$29a647f1-2014-533c-bc6b-281e71733fbe$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 25 · Licensing$ml$, $ml$Getting a US imaging satellite to work involves three federal licenses. The FAA licenses the launch, the FCC licenses the satellite's radio signals, and the Commerce Department licenses private remote sensing systems. The reason goes back to the 1967 Outer Space Treaty: countries answer for their companies in space, so private missions need authorization and continuing supervision.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.faa.gov/space", "label": "FAA, commercial space transportation"}, {"url": "https://www.satellitetoday.com/government-military/2022/09/30/fcc-adopts-5-year-rule-for-deorbiting-satellites/", "label": "Via Satellite, FCC five-year deorbit rule"}, {"url": "https://space.commerce.gov/regulations/commercial-remote-sensing-regulatory-affairs/", "label": "Office of Space Commerce, remote sensing licensing"}, {"url": "https://www.unoosa.org/documents/pdf/spacelaw/activities/2020/SLC2020Presentations/SLC2020PDFPresentations/A._Newman_-_8_Dec_2020_-_Fundamentals_of_Space_Law_.pdf", "label": "UNOOSA, fundamentals of space law"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$f668ff32-9233-5f03-82bb-1bb6afd8f9e8$ml$::uuid, $ml$29a647f1-2014-533c-bc6b-281e71733fbe$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$License 1 · Launch$ml$, $ml$The FAA licenses launches and reentries. Its job is protecting the public on the ground and in the air.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.faa.gov/space", "label": "FAA, commercial space transportation"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$9821c1b1-09db-5b66-83f1-63e28e33255c$ml$::uuid, $ml$29a647f1-2014-533c-bc6b-281e71733fbe$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$License 2 · Spectrum$ml$, $ml$The FCC licenses the radio signals a satellite uses. It also sets rules like the five-year deorbit limit.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.satellitetoday.com/government-military/2022/09/30/fcc-adopts-5-year-rule-for-deorbiting-satellites/", "label": "Via Satellite, FCC five-year deorbit rule"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$c12f72a0-0429-5be0-a9b3-8b26581e52bd$ml$::uuid, $ml$29a647f1-2014-533c-bc6b-281e71733fbe$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Imaging needs a third license$ml$, $ml$Private operators of remote sensing satellites are licensed by Commerce's Office of Space Commerce.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://space.commerce.gov/regulations/commercial-remote-sensing-regulatory-affairs/", "label": "Office of Space Commerce, remote sensing licensing"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$1f349f8f-2a42-5387-beea-abfa24169877$ml$::uuid, $ml$29a647f1-2014-533c-bc6b-281e71733fbe$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Know the license map$ml$, $ml$Name the three US licenses: FAA for launch, FCC for spectrum, Commerce for imaging. Few candidates can.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.faa.gov/space", "label": "FAA, commercial space transportation"}, {"url": "https://www.satellitetoday.com/government-military/2022/09/30/fcc-adopts-5-year-rule-for-deorbiting-satellites/", "label": "Via Satellite, FCC five-year deorbit rule"}, {"url": "https://space.commerce.gov/regulations/commercial-remote-sensing-regulatory-affairs/", "label": "Office of Space Commerce, remote sensing licensing"}]$ml$::jsonb),
