($ml$66e11958-1302-5ae6-81e9-2bfcdb6eb79e$ml$::uuid, $ml$8099728c-b19a-5fd7-9c51-eb8c77997516$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 28 · The numbers$ml$, $ml$Since 2019, satellite constellations must deploy 10% within 2 years, 50% within 5 and all within 7. The International Telecommunication Union set these milestones for non-geostationary systems at its 2019 World Radiocommunication Conference. The clock starts after the regulatory period for bringing frequencies into use ends. The goal is to keep the master frequency register close to what is actually flying and to stop spectrum warehousing.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://itu.int/en/mediacentre/backgrounders/Pages/Non-geostationary-satellite-systems.aspx", "label": "ITU, non-geostationary satellite systems"}]$ml$::jsonb),
