($ml$16a14a7a-0178-51c4-a1aa-4fabd8ac23db$ml$::uuid, $ml$74d1dfcc-78b0-516c-803b-9442ceeff2cb$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In space, spectrum is reserved on paper but kept by launching.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://itu.int/en/mediacentre/backgrounders/Pages/Non-geostationary-satellite-systems.aspx", "label": "ITU, non-geostationary satellite systems"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$401daff3-2588-5bb8-a2df-bc6710b5998f$ml$::uuid, $ml$9a9eafcf-3d41-5a39-a208-cb93b3c30e50$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 29 · The rule$ml$, $ml$In January 2018, Swarm Technologies launched four tiny satellites the FCC had refused to approve. The SpaceBEEs, about a quarter the size of a standard cubesat, flew on India's PSLV. The FCC had worried they would be too hard to track. In December 2018, Swarm agreed to pay $900,000 and accept extra oversight, including reporting each launch deal to the FCC.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://techcrunch.com/2018/12/20/fcc-fines-swarm-technologies-900k-over-unauthorized-satellite-launch/", "label": "TechCrunch, FCC fines Swarm $900K"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$f39d6abf-f52b-5f3b-a595-a7c78543f29c$ml$::uuid, $ml$9a9eafcf-3d41-5a39-a208-cb93b3c30e50$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The concern$ml$, $ml$Too small to track was the problem. Satellites nobody can track raise collision risk for everyone.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://techcrunch.com/2018/12/20/fcc-fines-swarm-technologies-900k-over-unauthorized-satellite-launch/", "label": "TechCrunch, FCC fines Swarm $900K"}]$ml$::jsonb),
