($ml$201084f3-fd97-5b6b-8a6f-215f74c04cff$ml$::uuid, $ml$c6d2a492-075e-56e2-bc74-c4f592274ae8$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In space, launching without a license costs more than waiting for one.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://techcrunch.com/2018/12/20/fcc-fines-swarm-technologies-900k-over-unauthorized-satellite-launch/", "label": "TechCrunch, FCC fines Swarm $900K"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$cf465bd2-d90b-5101-bc90-7f536d358c84$ml$::uuid, $ml$a2ac8843-2bcc-5622-ad57-3982d2619c04$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 30 · Where it breaks$ml$, $ml$In September 2021, Rwanda filed at the ITU for a constellation of 327,320 satellites. The filing, called CINNAMON-937, spread the satellites across 27 orbital shells. It was not clear who would build them. Filings like this reserve frequencies on paper long before anything flies, which is why the ITU added deployment milestones in 2019.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://spaceinafrica.com/2021/10/14/rwanda-has-submitted-itu-filing-for-27-orbital-shells-of-327320-satellites/", "label": "Space in Africa, Rwanda's ITU filing"}, {"url": "https://itu.int/en/mediacentre/backgrounders/Pages/Non-geostationary-satellite-systems.aspx", "label": "ITU, non-geostationary satellite systems"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$76eaab05-3463-5473-ad6b-92e50455ad72$ml$::uuid, $ml$a2ac8843-2bcc-5622-ad57-3982d2619c04$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The scale$ml$, $ml$The filing dwarfs anything in orbit. Starlink had about 9,400 active satellites in early 2026.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://spaceinafrica.com/2021/10/14/rwanda-has-submitted-itu-filing-for-27-orbital-shells-of-327320-satellites/", "label": "Space in Africa, Rwanda's ITU filing"}, {"url": "https://teslanorth.com/2026/01/25/starlink-satellites-made-300000-moves-to-avoid-collisions-in-2025", "label": "TeslaNorth, citing SpaceX filing to the FCC"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$cfb0af80-0d64-5267-a973-53a37e69658c$ml$::uuid, $ml$a2ac8843-2bcc-5622-ad57-3982d2619c04$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The problem$ml$, $ml$Paper filings blur the picture of what will really fly. The ITU's milestones aim to keep its register close to reality.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://itu.int/en/mediacentre/backgrounders/Pages/Non-geostationary-satellite-systems.aspx", "label": "ITU, non-geostationary satellite systems"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$ac4399cb-f20c-5293-bcfe-cb3a42de6395$ml$::uuid, $ml$a2ac8843-2bcc-5622-ad57-3982d2619c04$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Telling real from paper$ml$, $ml$Regulators, investors and operators all need better ways to judge which filings will actually launch. A subset, CINNAMON-217, alone covered 52,080 satellites.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://spaceinafrica.com/2021/10/14/rwanda-has-submitted-itu-filing-for-27-orbital-shells-of-327320-satellites/", "label": "Space in Africa, Rwanda's ITU filing"}, {"url": "https://itu.int/en/mediacentre/backgrounders/Pages/Non-geostationary-satellite-systems.aspx", "label": "ITU, non-geostationary satellite systems"}]$ml$::jsonb),
